---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const description =
  'About Bycon and our transport management platform: trip lifecycle, scheduling, communications, analytics, driver tools, and administration—built for broker-led and NEMT-style operations.';
---
<Layout title="About" description={description}>
  <article class="prose about-page">
    <h1>About Bycon</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      We build operations software for teams that move people—where schedules slip, documentation matters, and the record
      has to hold up after the trip is done. The capabilities below describe our transport management platform as it exists
      in the product today; your deployment can vary by configuration and integrations.
    </p>
    <p class="disclaimer">
      Capabilities depend on configuration, roles, and integrations. Nothing here is a legal or regulatory guarantee—review
      with counsel where compliance obligations apply.
    </p>

    <nav class="about-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <span class="about-toc-label">On this page</span>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
        <li><a href="#trips">Trips &amp; demand</a></li>
        <li><a href="#scheduling">Scheduling &amp; routing</a></li>
        <li><a href="#communication">Communication</a></li>
        <li><a href="#analytics">Analytics &amp; reporting</a></li>
        <li><a href="#workforce">Drivers &amp; workforce</a></li>
        <li><a href="#admin">Administration</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <section id="overview" class="about-section">
      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p>
        The platform is a <strong>multi-company transport operations system</strong> with role-based access for super
        administrators, company administrators, dispatchers, and drivers. It supports the arc from trip intake and planning
        through scheduling, execution, client and driver communication, and performance reporting—suited to broker-led and
        NEMT-style operations where trip history, timeliness, and defensible records matter.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="trips" class="about-section">
      <h2>Trip and demand management</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Trip lifecycle</strong> from broker-style assignment through scheduling and field outcomes—completed,
          canceled, no-show, combined, and related statuses as modeled in the product.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Create, search, filter, and edit trips</strong>, including operational preferences such as grouping,
          round trips, driver requirements, and assignment locking.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>CSV import</strong> with validation and company-level defaults (for example transportation provider).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Broker integration workflows</strong> where configured—such as Ecolane-oriented export/import and pushing run
          or vehicle assignments back to the broker system.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Dispatch-oriented tagging</strong> on trips for prioritization and coordination.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Blocked clients</strong> to prevent transport when policy or safety requires it.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="scheduling" class="about-section">
      <h2>Scheduling, routing, and optimization</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Route generation</strong> from daily trip sets using configurable optimization (including constraint-based
          routing and alternate planning modes), with extensive configuration—batching, wait limits, optimizer selection, and
          related parameters.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Day-level schedules and routes</strong>: view, adjust, regenerate, and re-optimize as the day changes.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Operational adjustments</strong> such as reassigning work, swapping drivers between routes, and related
          flows exposed through the scheduling API and UI.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Schedule periods</strong> and linkage to <strong>driver timesheets</strong> where the product ties work
          windows to payroll-style tracking.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="communication" class="about-section">
      <h2>Client and driver communication</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>SMS to clients</strong> for trip-related messaging—confirmations, reminders, cancellations, driver en
          route—including bulk sends with safeguards.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Driver SMS</strong>: broadcast and targeted messaging, with support for inbound driver replies where
          implemented.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Opt-out handling</strong> for SMS to respect subscriber preferences.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="analytics" class="about-section">
      <h2>Analytics and reporting</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Operations reporting</strong> over user-selected date ranges: trip volumes, status mix, mileage, on-time
          metrics, and driver performance summaries.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Focused report views</strong> in the application—including on-time, mileage, trip- and driver-level
          analyses, and compensation-oriented reporting where role permissions allow.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="workforce" class="about-section">
      <h2>Driver and workforce tools</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Driver records and documents</strong> with upload and expiry awareness (including UI alerts where wired).
        </li>
        <li><strong>Timesheets</strong>: driver submission and administrative review.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Driver-facing web experience</strong>: assigned routes, schedule visibility, timesheets, and
          documents—separate from the dispatcher console.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="admin" class="about-section">
      <h2>Administration and platform</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Per-company administration</strong>: users, settings, and integration credentials (such as broker
          credentials) managed in the product.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Super-administration</strong> of companies and cross-company users where applicable.
        </li>
        <li><strong>In-app notifications</strong> and Help / FAQ content.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Dispatcher shortcuts</strong>: natural-language style commands with rule-based interpretation and
          confirmation for destructive or sensitive actions—not a general-purpose open-ended assistant.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <p style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      For product access and positioning, see <a href="/solutions">Solutions</a>. To talk about fit for your network,
      <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.
    </p>
  </article>

  <style>
    .about-page {
      max-width: 46rem;
    }
    .about-page .disclaimer {
      font-size: 0.8125rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin: -0.25rem 0 1.25rem;
      padding: 0.65rem 0.85rem;
      background: var(--surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
    }
    .about-toc {
      margin: 0 0 2rem;
      padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
      background: var(--surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.04);
    }
    .about-toc-label {
      display: block;
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
    }
    .about-toc ul {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0.35rem 1rem;
      list-style: none;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
    }
    .about-toc li {
      margin: 0;
    }
    .about-toc a {
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      font-weight: 500;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: var(--accent);
    }
    .about-toc a:hover {
      color: var(--accent-hover);
      text-decoration: underline;
    }
    .about-section h2 {
      scroll-margin-top: 5rem;
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
